Once a BH forms and spins up due to disk accretion, it could conceivably power a relativistic jet capable of escaping the star (MacFadyen & Woosley, 1999). The power of the BZ jet from a Kerr BH of mass M_{\\rm BH} depends on both its (dimensionless) spin a_{\\rm BH} and the magnetic flux according to (Tchekhovskoy et al., 2011; Gottlieb et al., 2023):

